> Original seeded forty-vertex density study

Retain one mt19937_64 seed31 stream across thresholds10,20,...90. For each
separately generated forty-vertex graph, draw rng()%100 for every upper-triangle
pair and include the edge when below its threshold. Continue the stream rather
than reseeding or reusing one set of latent edge uniforms. The nominal
thresholds therefore describe separate samples, not a nested process of adding
edges to one graph. Their observed maximum sizes need not be monotone in
general.

Each plotted size is a completed exact native search. The table also reports
actual edge counts, entered frames and selected adjacency-test counts. They
measure this one stream/model, without a general average-case complexity or
scalability guarantee for arbitrary dense graphs.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/max_clique_density.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto rows = dm::algorithms::max_clique_density_study();
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| prescribed percent | actual distinct edges | completed exact search | actual maximum size " "| entered frames | actual colour adjacency tests | actual candidate adjacency tests |\n| " "---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &r : rows) {
        auto &a = r.analysis;
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", r.percent, a.edges,
                   a.complete, a.clique.size(), a.work.nodes,
                   a.work.colour_checks, a.work.candidate_checks);
        x.push_back(r.percent / 100.);
        y.push_back(a.clique.size());
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, y, "exact native size", {37, 99, 235});
    p.points(x, y, "", {37, 99, 235});
    p.legend({"exact native size"}, {{37, 99, 235}});
    p.x_label("prescribed separate-graph edge threshold").y_label(
        "actual completed maximum clique size").title("Original seed31: separate forty-vertex graphs").save_svg("build/max_clique_density.svg");
}
```
